desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Temp Dir"
	title_zh: "Temp Dir"
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-temp-dir"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `temp-dir` (rust/lang/security/temp-dir.yml).
Original message: temp_dir should not be used for security operations. From the docs: 'The temporary directory may be shared among users, or between processes with different privileges; thus, the creation of any files or directories in the temporary directory must use a secure method to create a uniquely named file. Creating a file or directory with a fixed or predictable name may result in “insecure temporary file” security vulnerabilities.'
CWE: CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision
References:
- https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/env/fn.temp_dir.html
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rs": <<<POS
std::env::temp_dir()
POS
	"safefile://pos.rs": <<<NEG
std::env::home_dir()
NEG
)

${*.rs}.pattern_regex(/(?:std::env::temp_dir\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Temp Dir",
	title_zh: "Temp Dir",
	message: "Temp Dir detected.",
}
